Renderer is core Three.js (`THREE.WebGLRenderer`).

Problem: `renderer` created on line 41, but `OrbitControls` use `renderer.domElement` on line 12. Variable not exist yet. Reference error.

Move `renderer` definition above `OrbitControls`:

```ts
  // Renderer
  const renderer = new THREE.WebGLRenderer();
  renderer.setPixelRatio(window.devicePixelRatio);
  container.appendChild(renderer.domElement);

  // Scene & Camera
  const camera = new THREE.PerspectiveCamera(75, window.innerWidth / window.innerHeight, 0.1, 1000);
  camera.position.z = 1;

  const controls = new OrbitControls(camera, renderer.domElement);
  controls.update();
```

*(Note: base `THREE.Camera()` has no projection matrix for orbit controls. Use `THREE.PerspectiveCamera` or `THREE.OrthographicCamera` if need orbit).*

