Vertex shader ignore camera matrices.

`vertex.glsl` hardcode `gl_Position = vec4(position, 1.0);`. Position go straight to clip space. Camera and OrbitControls have zero effect on mesh.

Two fixes:

### 1. Fix [vertex.glsl](file:///home/gaitano/01-studio/01-src/shaders/shader-template-react-ts/src/shader/vertex.glsl#L12)
Multiply position by Three.js built-in camera matrices:
```glsl
void main() {
    vUv = uv;
    gl_Position = projectionMatrix * modelViewMatrix * vec4(position, 1.0);
}
```

### 2. Update camera aspect in [scene.ts](file:///home/gaitano/01-studio/01-src/shaders/shader-template-react-ts/src/scene.ts#L50)
In `onWindowResize`:
```ts
function onWindowResize() {
  camera.aspect = window.innerWidth / window.innerHeight;
  camera.updateProjectionMatrix();
  renderer.setSize(window.innerWidth, window.innerHeight);
  // ...
}
```

Save files. Scroll wheel zoom now work.

